      "Step": "Legal & Operational Setup",
      "Description": "Address necessary local business registrations, food handling permits, and basic contract templates for potential franchise agreements or local partnerships.",
      "Deliverables": [
        "Checklist of Required Permits",
        "Basic operational SOP (Standard Operating Procedure) draft"
      ],
      "Priority": "Medium"
    },
    {
      "Step": "Digital Marketing Lead Generation Strategy",
      "Description": "Develop content plans specific to the target demographic in Asunción. Focus on 'experience' marketing (e.g., 'The Perfect Weekend Treat') rather than just product listing.",
      "Deliverables": [
        "30-day Content Calendar Draft",
        "Targeted Google/Instagram Ad Copy Sets"
      ],
      "Priority": "Medium"
    }
  ],
  "SummaryAdvice": "We are currently in the 'Build/Validate' phase. The next steps require parallel effort: build the digital *skeleton* while validating the physical *muscle* (the product and supply chain). Prioritizing the MVP and the COGS sheet simultaneously will keep momentum high and de-risk the entire launch."
}

{
  "action": "generate_plan",
  "plan_name": "MVP Development Plan for Stored Site Launch",
  "description": "This plan breaks down the next steps required to deploy a Minimum Viable Product (MVP) of the website, leveraging the existing architectural decisions (Next.js, TailwindCSS, Supabase/Supabase-like stack).",
  "steps": [
    {
      "step_number": 1,
      "step_name": "Finalize Hosting & Domain Linking",
      "details": "Select the definitive hosting platform (e.g., Vercel, Netlify) and ensure the correct subdomain pointing to the new deployment directory is active and resolves correctly.",
      "priority": "Critical",
      "deliverable": "Live, accessible development URL for the MVP."
    },
    {
      "step_number": 2,
      "step_name": "Database Schema Setup & Seeding",
      "details": "Deploy the final `schema.sql` to the production database instance (e.g., Supabase). Seed critical, static data needed for the MVP (e.g., core menu items, initial 'About Us' content, basic location details).",
      "priority": "High",
      "deliverable": "Populated production database ready to serve read requests."
    },
    {
      "step_number": 3,
      "step_name": "Develop Core Components (UI/UX Polish)",
      "details": "Refine the look and feel based on the final brand guidelines. Focus on: Hero section responsiveness, main navigation polish, and ensuring consistent use of Tailwind utilities across all components.",
      "priority": "Medium",
      "deliverable": "Visually polished, component-level development branch."
    },
    {
      "step_number": 4,
      "step_name": "Implement Core Functionality (MVP Scope)",
      "details": "Focus only on the absolute essential user journeys:\n1. **View Menu/Products:** Fetch and display dynamic product data from the DB.\n2. **Contact Form:** Basic form submission endpoint (requires backend/edge function).\n3. **About Page:** Display static content correctly.",
      "priority": "Critical",
      "deliverable": "Working, functional user paths (No checkout/booking required for MVP)."
    },
    {
      "step_number": 5,
      "step_name": "Testing & Quality Assurance (Internal Alpha)",
      "details": "Conduct rigorous testing across primary devices (mobile, tablet, desktop). Test form submissions, database reads, and general site speed/load times. Debug any client-side or server-side errors.",
      "priority": "Critical",
      "deliverable": "Bug-fixed, QA-approved staging environment."
    },
    {
      "step_number": 6,
      "step_name": "Final Deployment & Monitoring",
      "details": "Deploy the finalized build to the production domain. Set up basic analytics tracking (Google Analytics) and error monitoring (Sentry) before launching.",
      "priority": "Critical",
      "deliverable": "Publicly accessible, stable MVP website."
    }
  ],
  "next_action": "Proceed with Step 1: Finalize Hosting & Domain Linking."
}

